# LAND-ALPHA-BRUSH: UE Landscape Mode's Alpha and Pattern brush sets (FLandscapeBrushAlpha / AlphaPattern).
# The brush is weighed by one channel of a texture asset's SOURCE image, chosen from the palette.
# NEEDS an alpha image at Assets/Landscape/Alphas/Stamp_Ridge.png (a greyscale ridge/crater stamp, e.g. a UE-style
# landscape alpha); the palette row imports it into its .detex on the first choice.
Дано run Landscape "Manage mode"
Дано run Landscape "New Landscape: Create"
Дано run Landscape "Sculpt mode"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.6,-0.6,0.6
Дано run Landscape "Alpha texture: Landscape/Alphas/Stamp_Ridge.png"
Дано run Landscape "Brush type: Alpha"
Дано run Landscape "Auto-rotate: off"
Тогда-вид 0_flat the new landscape is flat; the Tool Settings show Brush Type Alpha, Auto-Rotate off, Texture Rotation 0
Когда run Landscape "Stroke at the viewport centre"
Тогда-вид 1_alpha the stamp's own shape (the ridge of Stamp_Ridge.png) rises at the centre, fitted inside the brush circle: not a round dome
Когда run Landscape "Texture rotation: +45"
Когда run Landscape "Stroke at the viewport centre"
Тогда-вид 2_rotated a second copy of the same stamp on top of the first, turned 45 degrees against it
Когда run Action "Undo"
Когда run Action "Undo"
Когда run Landscape "Brush type: Pattern"
Когда run Landscape "Texture scale: smaller"
Когда run Landscape "Stroke at the viewport centre"
Тогда-вид 3_pattern a round patch whose surface repeats the stamp as a tiled relief, fading to nothing at the brush edge (Smooth falloff)
Когда run Landscape "Pattern world-space: on"
Когда run Landscape "Stroke at the viewport centre"
Тогда-вид 4_world the patch now carries the pattern at its world-space repeat (3200 cm tiles): larger cells than in 3_pattern
Когда run Landscape "Brush type: Circle"
Когда run Action "Undo"
Когда run Action "Undo"
Тогда-вид 5_undo the landscape is flat again, as in 0_flat
